  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building in Effective Natural Resource Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Climate Risk Index ranks Pakistan among the top 10 countries most affected by climate change in the world. Whereas its share of global GHG emissions is only 0.93%. Recurrent intense disasters and changing weather patterns are increasingly affecting living conditions, livelihoods, and development across Pakistan &#x2013; including variations in precipitation and temperatures, glacial melt, glacial lake outburst floods, rising sea levels, loss of biodiversity, and prolonged drought. UNESCO sites like BRs and Geoparks provide excellent opportunities for testing innovative conservation and sustainable livelihood practices. The project intends to develop the capacities of stakeholders in effective natural resource management.</narrative>
  </description>
